@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
title C Process Memory Layout (High Level)

package "Process Virtual Memory" {
  [Text / Code\n(.text + .rodata)\nRead-only] as TEXT
  [Data Segment\nInitialized globals/statics] as DATA
  [BSS Segment\nUninitialized globals/statics\n(auto = 0)] as BSS
  [Heap\nmalloc/calloc/realloc\nGrows upward ↑] as HEAP
  [Stack\nFunction frames\nLocals, return address\nGrows downward ↓] as STACK
}

TEXT -down-> DATA
DATA -down-> BSS
BSS -down-> HEAP
HEAP -down-> STACK

note right of HEAP
Heap allocations persist until free()
Fragmentation may occur.
end note

note right of STACK
Each function call creates a stack frame.
Limited size (per thread).
end note

@enduml
